# Trimmed build log: run6 (offline, final)

Source: scratchpad `run6_offline_final.log`, 860,362 bytes / 7,868 lines
(offline Conan+CMake+Ninja build of the same R-package CMake target, with
`conan remote disable conancenter` and a pre-populated Conan cache/venv --
this is the run referenced by catboost-8z4.3-report.md as the "zero network"
build). This file keeps the compiler-detection/Conan-bootstrap header and the
final ~60 lines of the Ninja build; ~7,700 lines of per-target-file
`[NNNN/4265] Building/Linking ...` progress lines were cut.

Note: unlike run1's log, this capture starts mid-configure (compiler
identification already underway) -- the capture does not include the
top-of-log `cmake ...` invocation line itself. The invocation used for this
run is identical to run1's except for the offline Conan setup (remote
disabled, cache pre-populated) described in catboost-8z4.3-report.md; it is
not re-quoted here since it was not present in this particular capture.

